   * @param body Department creation data with required name, optional description, and optional parent department reference for hierarchical structure
   * @x-autobe-authorization-type null
   * @x-autobe-authorization-actor member
   * @x-autobe-specification Create department implementation:
   *
   * 1. Authorization: Verify the requesting member has 'organizations:write' or 'manage_organization' permission.
   *
   * 2. Input validation:
   *    - name: Required, non-empty string, max length 255, trimmed
   *    - description: Optional string, max length 2000, trimmed if provided
   *    - parentDepartmentId: Optional UUID string
   *
   * 3. Organization context: Extract organization_id from the authenticated member's session context. The API will use the organizationId from the member's current organization context.
   *
   * 4. Uniqueness validation: Query erp_hrm_departments to ensure no existing non-deleted record exists with the same organization_id and name (case-insensitive). Return 409 Conflict with clear error message if duplicate exists.
   *
   * 5. Parent department validation (if parentDepartmentId provided):
   *    - Verify parent department exists in the same organization
   *    - Verify parent department's parent_department_id is null (ensuring single-level nesting constraint per section 39)
   *    - Return 400 Bad Request if nesting constraint would be violated
   *
   * 6. Construction: Create new erp_hrm_departments record with:
   *    - id: Generate UUID v4
   *    - organization_id: From session context
   *    - parent_department_id: From request or null
   *    - name: Truncated and normalized name
   *    - description: Optional description
   *    - created_at/updated_at: Current timestamp
   *    - deleted_at: null
   *
   * 7. Return: The full IErpHrmDepartment including generated id and timestamps.
   * @nestia Generated by Nestia - https://github.com/samchon/nestia
   */
  @TypedRoute.Post()
  public async create(
    @MemberAuth()
    member: MemberPayload,
    @TypedBody()
    body: IErpHrmDepartment.ICreate,
  ): Promise<IErpHrmDepartment> {
    try {
      return await postErpHrmMemberDepartments({
        member,
        body,
      });
    } catch (error) {
      console.log(error);
      throw error;
    }
  }

  /**
   * Retrieve a filtered and paginated list of departments within the current organization.
   *
   * This operation provides department browsing capabilities for all organization members, enabling them to understand the organizational structure and identify appropriate contacts or reporting lines. The department list displays each department's name, description, and hierarchical position.
   *
   * Departments support one level of parent-child nesting to model hierarchical team structures. Top-level departments (those without a parent) appear as primary organizational units, with their child departments displayed as subordinate units.
   *
   * Search capabilities include partial name matching using full-text search, filtering by parent department to view specific branches of the hierarchy, and standard pagination for organizations with many departments. The response includes summary information optimized for list displays, with parent department references for hierarchical context.
