   *
   * This operation requires organization management permission.
   *
   * @param connection
   * @param departmentId Target department's unique identifier
   * @param body Department update data with fields to modify
   * @x-autobe-authorization-type null
   * @x-autobe-authorization-actor member
   * @x-autobe-specification Lookup the target department by departmentId from the erp_hrm_departments table ensuring it belongs to the current organization context and is not soft-deleted.
   *
   * Validate the requesting user has organization management permission for the current organization context.
   *
   * If updating the name field:
   * - Check for uniqueness constraint violation using @@unique([organization_id, name])
   * - Reject if another department in the same organization already has the requested name
   *
   * If updating the parentDepartmentId field:
   * - Validate the new parent department exists and belongs to the same organization
   * - Validate the new parent does not already have a parentDepartmentId set (enforcing single-level nesting constraint per requirements)
   * - Reject if attempting to create nesting deeper than one level
   * - Clear parentDepartmentId to make this a top-level department if null is provided
   *
   * Apply updates to name, description, and parentDepartmentId fields.
   *
   * Update the updated_at timestamp to current time.
   *
   * Fetch and return the updated department entity with its organization and parentDepartment relationships populated.
